{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/33862-htr-wto-dennis-maxwell-carpenter-and-other-questions","id":33862,"title":"[HtR][WtO] Dennis Maxwell \"Carpenter.\" and other questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-20T07:46:07-08:00","id":33862,"title":"[HtR][WtO] Dennis Maxwell \"Carpenter.\" and other questions","content":"Ever since my players started their campaing of Hunter The Reckoning, they been afraid of One Character in the whole OWoD cosmology. His Name is Dennis Maxwell, &quot;Carpenter.&quot;<br /> I started to read Wraith and i was wondering a couple of things.<br /> Which would be Carpenter's Stats, phatos etc...<br /> <br /> Second, Can a risen come back to the Skinlands to bring more havock?<br /> <br /> Third: now my players are currently playing Demon The Fallen... i wanted to know whats the perspective of the wraiths on the Fallen ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T08:58:03-08:00","id":33897,"title":"","content":"There's really only two, well three books you will need to create Carpenter, The WtO Rulebook, 2nd preferred, the Risen supplement and a copy of a VtM rulebook. Why the last one? Well you see the Risen can use a couple of the basic Disciplines but unfortunately the book on the Risen doesn't actually give those Disciplines, it assumes that you must already have VtM. Easily the dumbest mistake of the book.<br /> <br /> I don't have the Risen book with me at the moment and I can't remember off the top of my head what Arcanoi Rise can use so I can't help you there. But his fetters are a hammer (a weapon he used in life) and his former girlfriend who was involved in his death though she obviously died of the course of events in the HtR book he appeared so she may no longer be around depending on when you set your game. As for Attributes and Abilities given with what we've seen of him I'd have his Primary Attribute as Physical, followed by Mental and then Social. As for Abilities he was a mafia hitman so it should be obvious what kinds of things he should have dots in. But it's also clear that he's picked a decent amount of knowledge on wraiths and the Underworld so might also what to give him a couple of dots in an Extra Knowledge on the Underworld or wraiths.<br /> <br /> Second Question: Carpenter did so it is possible. But I don't remember what it says in the Risen book.<br /> <br /> Third Question: Unknown as the Sixth Great Maelstrom that ended WtO also freed the Fallen so there haven't been any WtO books that talk about demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:04:19-08:00","id":33901,"title":"","content":"sorry, as for the second i misstyped, Can a risen (who got recently destroyed) Come back from the Shadowlands to mess around the skinlands still?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:12:29-08:00","id":33905,"title":"","content":"That's what I assumed when I answered. It's been a long time since I've read the Risen book so I don't remember but I do know that Carpenter did come back to the Skinlands after going through the Harrowing shown in HtR's The Walking Dead book so I assume it is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:16:05-08:00","id":33906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/33862-htr-wto-dennis-maxwell-carpenter-and-other-questions?p=33901#post33901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sorry, as for the second i misstyped, Can a risen (who got recently destroyed) Come back from the Shadowlands to mess around the skinlands still?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Before The Reckoning era, it was harder for Risen to be created. The events leading up to that blasted thousands of Wraiths across the Shroud and into bodies, often not their own. It also caused enough damage to the Shroud to make it easier for Wraiths to return as Risen. The only issue you'd run into there is whether or not the Wraith was destroyed in the event that shot him back into the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> There's more info, if you're interested, in the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/123/Ends-of-Empire?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ends of Empire</a> book for Wraith.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, as far as the powers of a Risen are concerned, I forget the title, but there is a Hunter ST book (one of the thin, paperback ones) that has the list of various powers the different kinds of creatures can use. Just draw from that pool of powers for something that seems appropriate and save yourself the money on buying a Vampire corebook just for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-20-2013, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T10:40:57-08:00","id":34499,"title":"","content":"my players fought him yesterday but he ran away.if they destroy his featters...he wont be able to return to the skinlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T14:14:31-08:00","id":34607,"title":"","content":"You really should get the Risen book because it does answer a lot of this.<br /> <br /> While a Risen will have several fetters, they have one that is more important, their Conduit. The Conduit is their big link between worlds. Destroy that and it's all over for them, at least as a Risen. They may manage to survive and continue existing as a wraith. But at the same time the Risen know how important the Conduit is and <i>will</i> protect it at all costs. And chances are Carpenter keeps it on himself, the hammer or another item of importance to him, so they'd have to get them from him first. That's not an easy task given how tough full on Risen like him can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:00:24-08:00","id":34981,"title":"","content":"Trivia note: Carpenter was actually Andrew Bates' player-character in the in-house playtest campaign we did for The Beast, aka Wraith 2nd. The rest of the group never did quite figure out he was a Spectre...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:08:28-08:00","id":34983,"title":"","content":"hey Realdeadguy, any chances you can get in touch with andrew and ask him for Carpenter's Stats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:29:02-08:00","id":35004,"title":"","content":"Given it's been 18 years since Wraith 2e, it's doubtful Bates still has Carpenter's stats anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}